home=f'''<section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">FIELD EXPERIMENT 41 / WALKER LANE</span><h1>Follow the transfer.<br>Test the hypothesis.</h1><p class="lead">A new fault-confidence map built from the space between two structural populations—not from an old submission.</p><span class="pill warn">Research candidate · submission gate closed</span>{download_block()}<p class="fine">Freshly generated artifact. Not organizer-scored. Do not spend a weekly slot on this version.</p></div><div class="map-card"><img src="structural-map.png" alt="Study-area map showing mapped faults in gray and new transfer-corridor confidence in color"><div class="caption">01 / Structural position, not catalogue density. <a href="structural-map.png">Open map ↗</a></div></div></section>
<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><b>{A['trace_parts']:,}</b><span>Trace parts classified by strike</span></div><div class="stat"><b>{A['corridors']}</b><span>Accepted cross-family corridors</span></div><div class="stat"><b>{100*A['top5percent_positive_at_junction_fraction']:.1f}%</b><span>Top-confidence pixels at junctions</span></div><div class="stat"><b>0</b><span>Predicted pixels ≤200 m from catalogue</span></div></div>
<section class="section split"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE RESULT, WITHOUT THE SPIN</span><h2>Valid file.<br>Unproven discovery.</h2><p>The model passes the format, novelty-versus-H33, and junction-concentration checks. It does <strong>not</strong> pass a meaningful generalization gate. Whole-trace withholding leaves almost no supported predictions inside the held-out blocks.</p><a href="research.html#validation">Read the complete failed experiment →</a></div><div class="card"><span class="pill warn">HOLDOUT / DO NOT SUBMIT YET</span><h3>Mean blocked DTI ≈ 0</h3><p>Measured value: <code>{CV['means']['candidate']:.6e}</code>. Only fold 0 has nonzero prediction mass; folds 1–3 have none. Junction concentration is a design check, not independent discovery evidence.</p><p class="fine">The historical H33 raster is not a clean holdout comparator: its construction used the complete catalogue. No claim of beating 0.2778—or the current leader—is justified.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><span class="eyebrow">TWO GEOMETRIC CRITERIA</span><h2>From fault traces to a falsifiable prediction.</h2><div class="three"><article class="card"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Separate the populations</h3><p>Assign axial strike to NW or N/NNE geometry. Retain every classification, including ambiguous and source-slip-discordant traces.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Connect genuine endpoints</h3><p>Find the nearest N/NNE receiver within 5 km of an outward-facing NW endpoint. Reject connected fragments and boundary tips.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Check local orientation</h3><p>Compare a topographic tangent proxy with the geometrically closer population. No new magnetic, gravity, thermal, or conductivity transform.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section card"><div class="split"><div><span class="eyebrow">DOWNLOAD &amp; REPRODUCE</span><h2>One artifact. A complete audit trail.</h2><p>The static site serves the precomputed, verified model output. It does not claim to train a model in your browser.</p><a href="executive-summary.html">Submission instructions →</a></div><div><p><a href="downloads/classified-traces.csv">Every trace classification (CSV)</a><br><a href="downloads/corridors-utm11.geojson">Transfer corridors (projected GeoJSON)</a><br><a href="downloads/structural-audit.json">Junction &amp; novelty diagnostics</a><br><a href="downloads/holdout.json">Every validation fold</a><br><a href="{REPO}/actions/workflows/reproduce.yml">Rebuild pipeline on GitHub Actions</a></p></div></div></section>
<div class="feed" id="source-feed">Official leaderboard observed 2026-10-05: 0.3262, not the brief’s 0.3195. <a href="{LEADER}">Check official leaderboard ↗</a></div>'''
(DOCS/'index.html').write_text(page('Structural transfer, honestly tested',home))

executive=f'''<div class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">EXECUTIVE SUMMARY / SUBMISSION GUIDE</span><h1>Your GeoTIFF, ready to inspect.</h1><p class="lead">The file has been generated and independently re-opened. Download it directly—no conversion, editing, or model training is required.</p>{download_block()}<div class="notice"><strong>Do not submit this candidate yet.</strong><p>The blocked validation result is effectively zero and a clean historical-best comparison is unavailable. Format-valid does not mean scientifically validated or competitive. No weekly slot has been spent.</p></div>
<h2>Artifact identity</h2><p><strong>Filename</strong><br><code>{M['filename']}</code></p><p><strong>Unique submission name</strong><br><code>{M['submission_name']}</code></p><p><strong>Short note ({len(M['note'])} characters)</strong></p><div class="copybox"><code id="submission-note">{E(M['note'])}</code><button class="copy" data-copy="submission-note" type="button">Copy note</button></div><p class="fine">SHA-256: <code>{M['format']['sha256']}</code></p>
<section class="section"><h2>When a future candidate clears the gate</h2><ol><li>Review its <strong>clean, spatially blocked comparison</strong> against the current best. Require an improvement before spending one of the three weekly slots.</li><li>Download the single <code>.tif</code> using the button above. Do not upload the map PNG, HTML page, audit JSON, or a renamed document.</li><li>Sign in to <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/">DrivenData’s GEMS competition</a>, confirm eligibility and accept the official rules using your own account.</li><li>Open <strong>New submission</strong>. Under <strong>File to submit</strong>, choose the downloaded GeoTIFF. Use the unique name in your internal tracker and paste the short note into <strong>Note (optional)</strong>.</li><li>Submit only after the gate passes. Wait for the portal’s validation and score. Record the exact file hash, submission ID, note, and organizer-reported score. A local validator cannot guarantee portal acceptance.</li><li>Select one final submission for both prize rounds by the official deadline. Disclose AI assistance in the required narrative; eligibility and certifications must be completed by the participant.</li></ol><p>These steps follow the <a href="{PROBLEM}#submission-format">format specification</a> and <a href="https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/96647.pdf">official rules, §§3.2–3.5</a>.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Why this file avoids the range error</h2><p>Every one of its 12,279,160 stored values is finite, with minimum 0 and maximum {M['format']['max']:.6f}. There is no negative sentinel or NaN-valued nodata tag. Outside-footprint cells contain numeric zero <em>and</em> are null through an internal GeoTIFF mask matching the template. This reconciles the published null-outside requirement with safe numerical values.</p><p>The exact cause of your earlier portal error is unknown without the rejected bytes. Out-of-range sentinel values are one possible cause; NaN alone is not proven to be the cause. We verified the current file rather than guessing about the old one.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Rebuild rather than copy</h2><pre><code>bash scripts/download_competition_data.sh
.venv/bin/python scripts/prepare_data.py
.venv/bin/python scripts/run_pipeline.py
.venv/bin/python scripts/build_site.py</code></pre><p><a href="{REPO}/actions/workflows/reproduce.yml">Run the reproducibility workflow</a> or use the setup commands in the README. The geometry-only model is CPU-based; it does not require a GPU. Reproducing identical inputs intentionally gives the same content-addressed artifact, not an artificial “new” file made by renaming it.</p></section></div>'''
