sources_html=f'''<span class="eyebrow">SOURCE REGISTER / MANUAL REVIEW</span><h1>Evidence you can follow.</h1><p class="lead">Official observations, owner-reported history, and our measured results are separate evidence classes. Links are not a substitute for testing a geological hypothesis.</p>{table(['ID / source','Evidence class','Verified scope'],[[f'<a href="{url}">{id} · {E(title)}</a>',E(kind),E(claim)] for id,title,url,kind,claim in sources])}<section class="section"><h2>Input lineage</h2><p>Official INGENIOUS vector bytes were fetched on a GitHub runner, archive-tested and checksum-pinned. The archive and field definitions are preserved under <code>data/official/</code>. Core rasters came from owner mirrors pinned to commits and SHA-256 in <a href="{REPO}/blob/arena/5d5d8cc8-gemsdoe41/research/input-receipt.json">the input receipt</a>. Hash equality proves mirror integrity, not organizer authentication. No prior prediction raster enters the structural model.</p><p>The <a href="downloads/classified-traces.csv">trace table</a> preserves the original source fields, including slip sense, and distinguishes geometric family from measured kinematics. The <a href="downloads/corridors-utm11.geojson">corridor GeoJSON</a> is explicitly projected UTM11, not RFC 7946 longitude/latitude; use QGIS with EPSG:32611.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>39 related sites, audited</h2><p>All 39 supplied website source files were retrieved through the GitHub contents API and inspected for primary-download, holdout, and score claims. This is a source-level audit, not an exhaustive rerun of every project or verification of every claimed score. Placeholders 40–44 in the brief have no supplied site or result.</p><p><a href="related-sites.json">Complete source hashes and claim excerpts (JSON)</a> · <a href="score-ledger.csv">All submission scores reported in the brief (CSV)</a></p>{table(['Project','Source audit','Evidence class'],[[f'<a href="{r["url"]}">{E(r["repo"])}</a>',E(r['status']),'Owner-authored; no organizer artifact receipt'] for r in related])}</section><section class="section"><h2>Refresh status</h2><p id="source-feed">Checked via research tools on 2026-10-05. Daily public-source checks run through GitHub Actions after merge.</p><p><a href="source-feed.json">Timestamped feed JSON</a> · <a href="{REPO}/actions/workflows/site.yml">Source-refresh and Pages run history</a></p><p>Fetch failures are published as errors and no score is invented. Source availability and scientific truth are different checks. This site does not collect logins, use hidden labels, or upload to DrivenData.</p></section>'''
(DOCS/'sources.html').write_text(page('Verified sources & related-site audit',sources_html))

# Preserve all supplied experiment IDs, including unscored entries, in an auditable ledger.
brief=(ROOT/'README.md').read_text().split('<summary>Read the complete original prompt</summary>',1)[1]
rows=[];current=None;seen=set()
for line in brief.splitlines():
    m=re.search(r'https://buffedlizard55-lab.github.io/([^/]+)/',line)
    if m:current=m.group(1)
    match=re.fullmatch(r'([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]+):\s*(0\.\d+)?',line.strip())
    if match and current:
        key=(current,match.group(1))
        if key not in seen:
            rows.append([current,match.group(1),match.group(2) or '', 'user-reported; not independently artifact-authenticated']);seen.add(key)
with (DOCS/'score-ledger.csv').open('w') as f:
    w=csv.writer(f);w.writerow(['project','submission_id','reported_score','evidence_class']);w.writerows(rows)
